&lt;p&gt;We are looking for an enthusiastic Electronics Engineering Intern to gain hands-on experience designing, building, testing, and debugging electronic hardware. Working alongside senior engineers, you’ll contribute across the development cycle—from schematic and PCB design through prototyping, testing, debugging, and documentation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities and Duties&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build, assemble, test, and debug prototype circuits and PCB assemblies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist with schematic capture and PCB design.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use lab equipment such as oscilloscopes, multimeters, power supplies, and signal generators for testing and troubleshooting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support soldering, rework, and other hands-on laboratory activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and test firmware for microcontrollers and embedded systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyse test results and document designs, tests, and project progress.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with senior engineers to troubleshoot technical issues and improve hardware performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Follow engineering and laboratory safety procedures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications and Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Currently pursuing a Master’s degree in Electrical/Electronics Engineering or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of analog and digital circuit design.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with PCB design tools such as Altium, KiCad, or Eagle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with electronics lab equipment and basic soldering.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Programming experience in C, C++, Python, or similar.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with STM32, ESP32, Arduino, or other microcontrollers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of communication protocols such as I²C, SPI, UART, CAN, or USB is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong problem-solving, communication, and teamwork skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience through university, robotics, or personal electronics projects is highly valued.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;EU citizenship required.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible working hours&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous holiday allowance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Car parking&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enhanced maternity &amp;amp; paternity leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mental health and wellbeing support&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Auterion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are building the leading software platform for AI-powered autonomous systems for enterprise and government customers. Our team is supporting the most important missions and solving the most challenging problems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Auterion, we bring together the sharpest minds who love to solve the hardest problems. Join a vibrant team built on innovation, openness, and excellence, where you’ll be empowered to develop ideas, collaborate across all levels, and make an impact that matters.&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>
